Further changes in this fork (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

This repository is a fork of bertholomus/TensorFold at commit 808eb4a (https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold), which is
itself a fork of ashhart/TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold). Changes below by Kristian Aaron (Krishando),
Copyright 2026. They let the deepseek_v41 family serve packs whose routed experts are EXL3 at mixed widths (2-5 bits per
expert) while attention, shared experts and head stay in DeepSeek's own FP8/bf16, as used by
https://huggingface.co/Krishando/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-EXL3-2.86bpw. Everything above this section is unchanged.

Added:
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/native_fp8.py          DeepSeek's own FP8 projections on the MXFP8 kernels
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/native_fp4_experts.py  DSpark draft experts in the checkpoint's own MXFP4
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/suffix_draft.py        context suffix drafts beside DSpark (TF_DS_SUFFIX_DRAFT)
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/memwatch.py            memory low-water logging and floor (TF_DS_MEMWATCH)
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/display_mem.py         optional, off by default (TF_DS_DISPLAY_EMBED); needs an
                                                                   external DRM helper that is not part of this repository
  docs/cebu-native-fp8-port.md                                     design notes for the native FP8 port
  recipes/dsv41-2spark/                                            Dockerfile, launch script and README for the release
  tools/dsv41/decision_kld.py                                      closeness to the full model at an agent's decision points

Modified upstream files:
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/weights.py   loads native FP8 linears and mixed-width EXL3 experts
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/model.py     builds the native FP8 / MXFP4 modules where the pack has them
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/engine.py    suffix drafts, memory watch and warm-up wiring
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/multi.py     suffix-draft and memory-watch hooks in the round
  src/tensorfold/families/deepseek_v41/cuda/dspark.py    native MXFP4 draft experts
  src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma.py, src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma_gather.cu   small fixes for the two-Spark link
  tools/dsv41/draft_bench.py, tools/dsv41/round_cost.py  benchmark clients follow the changes above
  README.md                                              a note above the existing fork note

"git log 808eb4a..HEAD" shows every change in this fork, and each added or modified file says so in its first line.
